inflation is at a 40-year high in the  united states and most market commentary  is focused on things like supply chain  disruptions geopolitical conflict and  other easy to blame causes but most  folks they don't actually acknowledge  that market intervention is one of the  leading causes of inflation  we had historic monetary stimulus in  2020 and 2021 and that led to historic  inflation but this is not a new concept  milton friedman the well-respected  economist and nobel prize winner  famously said inflation is always and  everywhere a monetary phenomenon in the  sense that it is and can be produced  only by a more rapid increase in the  quantity of money than an output this  idea of a monetary phenomenon is  something that milton friedman talked  about often here's a video of him from  decades ago talking about why inflation  is created in washington  inflation is made in washington because  only washington can create money  and any other attribution of two other  groups of inflation  is wrong  consumers don't produce it  producers don't produce it  the trade unions don't produce it  foreign sheiks don't produce it  oil imports don't produce it what  produces it is too much government  spending and too much government  creation of money and nothing else  don't take milton friedman's word for it  though if we go ahead and we take the m2  money supply and we lay it over the  actual inflation rate what we see is  that the m2 money supply explodes  upwards and shortly after we continue to  see higher inflation  but if we take a look deeper at that m2  money supply over the last 25 years the  name of the game has been create more  money and if we zoom in here on the last  five years we can see that the problem  is only getting worse and more magnified  there's no secret that the covet 19  pandemic led to government mandated  lockdowns which led to a liquidity  crisis and the velocity of money  dropping and so the government whether  right or wrong they decided to step in  and use monetary stimulus to get asset  prices and markets recovered but as  milton friedman also pointed out the  government solution to a problem is  usually as bad as the problem itself  that sounds eerily accurate given the  current situation that we're facing  as we look at the bureau of labor  statistics data we can see that the cpi  metric continues to accelerate moving  from about five and a half percent in  june of 2021 to now over 9  in june of 2022 but contrary to popular  belief disinflation is not the fault of  millennials it's also not the fault of  boomers or any other generation either  milton friedman knew this he's a very  interesting person to pay attention to  because he understood inflation  intimately he had a number of different  warnings that he issued over the years  and he even predicted environments like  we're living through right now one of  his most famous points was that  inflation is taxation without  legislation it simply steals from the  bottom 50 or so of americans and you  have no say there's no ability to vote  those who created it out of office and  you simply have to watch as your wealth  and your economic value is eroded away  by an invisible threat milton friedman  also has one of my favorite quotes ever  in this one he states  when government in pursuit of good  intentions tries to rearrange the  economy legislate morality or help  special interests the costs come in  inefficiency lack of motivation and loss  of freedom  government should be a referee  not an active player  now what we have watched is that central  banks and elected officials they can't  simply sit by and be the referee they've  been dying to be an active player  they've manipulated interest rates down  and now they're manipulating them back  up they were asset buyers with a  persistent bid in the market for years  and now they claim that they're going to  be an asset seller they're going to  shrink the federal reserve's balance  sheet  regardless of whether you believe them  or not what we are watching is that more  intervention equals more problems the  free market is smarter than politicians  we should allow the free market to work  milton friedman warned us about high  inflation and the problems that come  from market intervention  in fact  friedman didn't just warn us he  predicted this he saw what happens when  central banks can't simply help  themselves when they continue to  increase the monetary supply  and they don't allow for demand to catch  up  what we have lived through over the last  two years was an insane undisciplined  monetary and fiscal policy regime  and demand didn't grow fast enough  instead we are left with an ever  increasing monetary supply and now we  have historically high inflation  since 40 years ago we haven't seen  inflation like this  we have major problems in this country  and abroad  and unless central bankers and  politicians learn to stay out of the  market to allow the free market to do  its thing  we are only going to keep kicking the  can down the road and introducing more  and more problems milton friedman won  the nobel prize for a reason he  understood economics he understood free  markets and he understood inflation  it's about time that we start paying  attention to the lessons that he taught  us decades ago  because they're ever as relevant today  as they were back then
 

